<setup>
  <selectFromSequence name="a" from="2" to="5" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="b" from="8" to="12" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="c" from="2" to="4" step="1" exclude="$a"/>

  <function name="v" variable="t">$b - $a*t</function>
  <function name="s" variable="t">$c + $b*t - $a*t^2/2</function>

  <selectFromSequence name="p" from="1" to="3" step="1"/>
  <selectFromSequence name="q" from="4" to="6" step="1"/>

  <derivative name="dsEntdx" variable="x">$sEnt</derivative>
  <derivative name="dsEntdt" variable="t">$sEnt</derivative>

</setup>

<p>
  Suppose that an object moving along a straight line has its velocity given by the function 
  <me>
    v(t) = $v
  </me>
  with units meters per second for <m>0 \le t \le <math simplify>$q+2</math></m>.  In addition, suppose we know that <m>s(0) = $c</m>.
</p>

<p>
  <ol marker="a.">
    <li>
      <p>
        Recall that the object's position function, <m>s(t)</m>, is an antiderivative of its velocity, <m>v(t)</m>.  That is, <m>s'(t) = v(t)</m>.  Find a function <m>s(t)</m> for which <m>s'(t) = $v</m> and <m>s(0) = $c</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer name="sEnt"><label><m>s(t) = </m> </label>$s</answer>
      </p>
      <feedback condition="$dsEntdx !=0 and $sEnt.justSubmitted">Make sure your function uses the variable <m>t</m>, not <m>x</m>.</feedback>
      <feedback condition="$dsEntdt=$v and $sEnt.creditAchieved!= 1">You entered an antiderivative of <m>v(t)</m>, but it doesn't satisfy the condition that <m>s(0)=$c</m>.</feedback>
    </li>
    <li sectionWideCheckWork>
      <p>
        Use the position function to find the object's change in position on <m>[$p, $q]</m>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><mathInput minWidth="20"><label>The object's position at <m>t=$q</m> is <m>s($q)=</m></label></mathInput>$$s($q)</answer>meters.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><mathInput minWidth="20"><label>The object's position at <m>t=$p</m> is <m>s($p)=</m></label></mathInput>$$s($p)</answer>meters.
      </p>
      <p>
        <answer><mathInput minWidth="20"><label>The object's change in position on <m>[$p, $q]</m> is </label></mathInput>$$s($q)-$$s($p)</answer>meters.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <p>
        Use the position function to also find the object's total distance traveled on <m>[$p, $q]</m>.
      </p>
      <p sectionWideCheckWork>
        <answer><label>The object's total distance traveled on <m>[$p, $q]</m> is </label>
          <conditionalContent>
            <case condition="$b/$a < $q and $b/$a > $p">
              2*$$s($b/$a)-$$s($q)-$$s($p)
            </case>
            <else>abs($$s($q)-$$s($p))</else>
          </conditionalContent></answer> meters.
      </p>
      <hint>Be careful to take into account if velocity is sometimes (or always) negative.  When does <m>v(t)=0</m>?  Is that within the relevant interval?</hint>
    </li>
  </ol>
</p>